#.  maximum of
#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:189
#, no-wrap
msgid "For hire"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:195
msgid ""
"Mercenary units are very popular in the Old World.  Each army list may add "
"(hire) a maximum of 1 Regiments of Renown unit for each full 1000 points of "
"army value following the <<allies-table>>.  Hired units count towards the "
"maximum allowance per 1000 points of the unit type indicated in the <<hiring-"
"regiments-of-renown>> section."
msgstr ""

#.  remove type
#.  the extra
#.  or heroes
#.  magic items.
#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:200
#, no-wrap
msgid "Led by the Hero"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:207
msgid ""
"To represent the presence of a strong leader, Regiments of Renown units "
"(including artillery and heroes) cost 10 points more than their equivalents "
"in the standard armies (the extra point value is included in the Regiments "
"of Renown unit profile). They also receive a +1 bonus to the combat Attack "
"value of one stand. Note that this gives +1 Attack in total, not +1 to each "
"stand! This extra attack is not included in the Army Selector profile."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:209
msgid ""
"No magic items may be given to hired Regiments of Renown units or heroes."
msgstr ""

#.  humanised
#.  a lot → greatly
#.  stay independent → are unaffected by
#.  a separate Blunder
#.  remove just
#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:215
#, no-wrap
msgid "Independent and Exclusive"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:220
msgid ""
"Mercenaries recruit from many races and lands of the Old World. Living in "
"the Empire greatly ‘humanised’ them, but they still stay individual. "
"Therefore, they are unaffected by any army or racial special rules – neither "
"bonuses nor drawbacks."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:226
msgid ""
"Hired units can be ordered and brigaded without penalties, just like the "
"other units in your army. In case of a blunder make a separate Blunder roll "
"for Regiments of Renown units if they are brigaded with other troops. That "
"means one roll for your army list troops and one roll for Regiments of "
"Renown troops."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:230
msgid ""
"They may not be targeted by friendly Wizard’s spells and do not receive any "
"benefit from friendly spells or effects, including area spells and effects."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:236
msgid ""
"Additionally, your army may contain only one of each unique listed unit. If "
"your opponent hired the same regiment, roll a dice and decide who got the "
"‘authentic’ one and who the ‘impersonated’ one. This roll is just for fun, "
"without any impact in the game."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:239
#, no-wrap
msgid "Unit rules"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:269
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[dense-terrain,†2]]2. Dense Terrain"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:272
msgid ""
"Lumpin Croop’s Fighting Cocks are well used to sneaking about in woods and "
"bushes. No command penalty is applied to this unit on account of dense "
"terrain."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:273
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[throwing-weapons,†3]]3. Throwing weapons"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:276
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[undead,†4]]4. Undead"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:278
msgid ""
"The Cursed Company is undead, and as such the following rules apply to them:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:281
msgid ""
"They never act on initiative. The unit only moves in the Command phase if "
"given orders."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:284
msgid "They are unaffected by the −1 Command penalty for enemy within 20cm."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:287
msgid ""
"They are unaffected by the −1 Combat penalty for fighting terrifying troops."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:290
msgid ""
"They are unaffected by the Confusion rule – they cannot become confused for "
"any reason."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:291
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[repeating-crossbows,†5]]5. Repeating crossbows"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:298
msgid ""
"Mengil Manhide’s Manflayers are equipped with repeating crossbows. They may "
"shoot once at ranges up to 30cm and twice at ranges up to 15cm. A unit of "
"three stands would therefore shoot 6 Attacks at a target within 15cm and 3 "
"Attacks at a target at greater ranges. They may shoot at enemies that charge "
"them – in which case they shoot 1 Attack per stand regardless of range."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:299
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[pistols,†6]]6. Pistols"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:305
msgid ""
"Long Drong’s Slayer Pirates carry pistols... loads of pistols! They have a "
"shooting range of only 15cm and 360° vision – stands in this unit can draw "
"line of sight from all edges for the purpose of evading and shooting, "
"including shooting at charging enemies. Note that this unit still needs Line "
"of Sight from its front edge to charge an enemy."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:306
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[ogres,†7]]7. Ogres"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:313
msgid ""
"Ogres flock to mercenaries for the chance of a good fight and as much as "
"they can eat. These creatures are notoriously fond of fresh human meat, "
"although they will eat practically anything that was once alive (or still "
"is). To represent this, if an Ogre unit can use its initiative to charge an "
"enemy unit of humans at the start of the Command phase then it must do so "
"(not Dwarfs, Elves etc.)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:314
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[light-cavalry,†8]]8. Light Cavalry"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:322
msgid ""
"Light cavalry formations have a great use among the mercenaries. They are "
"experts at outmaneuvering an enemy and harrying his flanks. Light cavalry "
"have a shooting range of only 15cm and 360° vision – stands in this unit can "
"draw line of sight from all edges for the purpose of evading and shooting, "
"including shooting at charging enemies. Note that this unit still needs Line "
"of Sight from its front edge to charge an enemy."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:323
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[birdmen,†9]]9. Birdmen"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:331
msgid ""
"Only half-mad nutters like Tileans would try to fly! The Birdmen wear insane "
"contraptions of light wood covered in canvas that are shaped like wings and "
"allow them to glide on the air currents. These ‘wings’ allow the Birdmen to "
"fly and still use their crossbows as normal. Because they are awkward "
"flyers, they can be pursued by any type of enemy troops.  Birdmen are based "
"facing the long edge of the base in the same way as other infantry."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:332
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[galloper-guns,†10]]10. Galloper Guns"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:336
msgid ""
"These are lighter artillery than Dwarf or Empire cannons; due to this they "
"are shorter ranged, but can make up for their lighter shot by producing a "
"higher volume of fire."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:342
msgid ""
"Galloper Guns move 20cm. All the normal rules for artillery apply as well as "
"the xref:rules:artillery-and-machines.adoc#cannons[Cannon] rules for "
"shooting (bounce through, no saves and reduction of cover values). Because "
"they are light guns they have a range of only 40cm. They still may shoot at "
"charging enemy by firing ‘grapeshot’ as normal."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:343
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[dragons,†11]]11. Dragons"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:346
msgid ""
"Asarnil rides a Dragon. The Dragon can fly, increasing its rider’s move to "
"100cm. An extra [.edit]#+3/3# Attacks are added (included in Asarnil’s "
"profile)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:353
msgid ""
"The Dragon can breath fire if the character has joined a unit that isn’t "
"engaged in combat.  The fire breath has a range of 20cm and can be directed "
"against one target as for normal shooting with 3 Attacks that are worked out "
"in the usual way."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:356
msgid "Additionally Asarnil causes terror in his enemies."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:360
#, no-wrap
msgid "Allies Table"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:365
#, no-wrap
msgid "include::partial$regiments-of-renown-allies-table.tsv[]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:368
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ⓐ"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:369
msgid ""
"Available for this army – see the <<hiring-regiments-of-renown>> section for "
"details."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:369
#, no-wrap
msgid "·"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:370
msgid "Not available for this army."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:374
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hiring Regiments of Renown"
msgstr ""

#.  In the whole section, p → points
#.  colon, "a bad idea"
#. type: delimited block * 4
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:385
msgid ""
"Each Regiments of Renown unit counts towards the maximum allowance per 1000 "
"points of the unit type indicated in this section. Additionally there are "
"some restrictions in hiring specified units: Dwarfs would never fight "
"together with Greenskins or Elves, and hiring _The Cursed Company_ together "
"with _The Witch Hunters_ is a bad idea."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:386
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hiring examples"
msgstr ""

#.  the, move 1000 point value
#. type: delimited block = 4
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:393
msgid ""
"The player hiring the _Alcatani Fellowship_ in a 1000 point value Dwarf army "
"may field up to one Ranger unit instead of up to two.  Rangers are the "
"highest point value limited infantry type unit in the Dwarf army."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:396
msgid ""
"The player hiring the _Marksmen of Miragliano_ in a Chaos army does not "
"restrict any of his units."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:400
msgid ""
"The player hiring _Braganza’s Besiegers_ in a Tomb Kings army may field up "
"to two monster types (chosen by the player)  instead of the three available "
"in the army list for every 1000 points."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:406
msgid ""
"The player hiring _Voland’s Venators_ in a High Elf army may field up to two "
"Chariot units instead of three in a 1000 point value army or five chariots "
"instead of six in a 2000 point value army.  Chariots are the highest point "
"value limited units of cavalry or chariot type in the High Elf army."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:410
msgid ""
"The player hiring _Asarnil the Dragonlord_ in a 1000 point Araby army can’t "
"field a Djinn monster mount as the limit is one per 1000 points. In a 2000 "
"point army player may field one Djinn instead of two."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:418
msgid ""
"Count as one highest point value limited infantry type unit. If not "
"available, hiring does not restrict taking other units. They count as 1 of "
"any monster type in a Tomb Kings army. The Lost Legion cannot be hired "
"together with _Tichi-Huichi’s Raiders_."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:423
msgid ""
"Counts as one highest point value limited infantry type unit. If not "
"available, hiring does not restrict taking other units. They count as 1 of "
"any monster type in a Tomb Kings army."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:427
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:446
msgid ""
"Count as one highest point value limited shooting infantry type unit. If not "
"available, hiring does not restrict taking other units."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:432
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:437
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:442
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:468
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:490
msgid ""
"Count as one highest point value limited infantry type unit. If not "
"available, hiring does not restrict taking other units. They count as 1 of "
"any monster type in a Tomb Kings army."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:443
#, no-wrap
msgid "Lumpin Croop’s Fighting Cocks"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:448
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:451
msgid "Hiring does not restrict taking other units."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:456
msgid ""
"Count as one highest point value limited infantry type unit. If not "
"available, hiring does not restrict taking other units. _The Cursed Company_ "
"cannot be hired together with _The Witch Hunters_."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:457
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mengil Manhide’s Manflayers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:463
msgid ""
"Count as one highest point value limited infantry type unit. If not "
"available, hiring does not restrict taking other units. They count as 1 of "
"any monster type in a Tomb Kings army. _Mengil Manhide’s Manflayers_ cannot "
"be hired together with _Arsanil the Dragonlord_, _Long Drong’s Slayer "
"Pirates_ or _Gotrek and Felix_ in any army, [.edit]#or together with# Dwarfs "
"in a Dogs of War army."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:464
#, no-wrap
msgid "Beorg Bearstruck and the Bearmen of Urslo"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:475
msgid ""
"Count as one highest point value limited infantry type unit. If not "
"available, hiring does not restrict taking other units. They count as 1 of "
"any monster type in a Tomb Kings army. Orcs cannot be hired together with "
"_Long Drong’s Slayer Pirates_ or _Gotrek and Felix_ in any army [.edit]#or "
"together with# Dwarfs in a Dogs of War army."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:482
msgid ""
"Count as one highest point value limited infantry type unit. If not "
"available, hiring does not restrict taking other units. They count as 1 of "
"any monster type in Tomb Kings army. Pirates cannot be hired together with "
"_Ruglud’s Armoured Orcs_, _Oglah Khan’s Wolfboyz_, _Mengil Manhide’s "
"Manflyers_ or _Arsanil the Dragonlord_."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:485
msgid "Count as one highest point value artillery type unit."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:494
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:502
msgid ""
"Count as one highest point value limited cavalry or chariot unit type. They "
"count as one Ranger unit in a Dwarf army, or as one Gutter Runners unit in a "
"Skaven army."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:495
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Birdmen of Catrazza"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:497
msgid "Count as one flying unit with size value 3 stands."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:508
msgid ""
"Count as one highest point value limited cavalry or chariot unit type. They "
"count as one Gutter Runners unit in a Skaven army. _Oglah Khan’s Wolfboyz_ "
"cannot be hired together with _Long Drong’s Slayer Pirates_ or _Gotrek and "
"Felix_ in any army [.edit]#or together with# Dwarfs in Dogs of War army."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:509
#, no-wrap
msgid "Asarnil the Dragonlord"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:514
msgid ""
"Counts as one Hero type [.edit]#character# and one of highest point value "
"Monstrous Mount type causing terror. _Arsanil_ cannot be hired together with "
"_Mengil Manhide’s Manflyers_, _Long Drong’s Slayer Pirates_ or _Gotrek and "
"Felix_ in any army [.edit]#or together with# Dwarfs in Dogs of War army."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:515
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tichi-Huichi’s Raiders"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:519
msgid ""
"Count as one highest point value limited cavalry or chariot unit type. They "
"count as one Ranger unit in a Dwarf army. Raiders cannot be hired together "
"with Pirazzo’s Lost Legion."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:524
msgid ""
"Count as one Hero type [.edit]#character#. They cannot be hired together "
"with _Ruglud’s Armoured Orcs_, _Oglah Khan’s Wolfboyz_, _Mengil Manhide’s "
"Manflyers_ or _Arsanil the Dragonlord_."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
